<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $196.3 mln Dec 10.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $196.3 mln Dec 10.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $196.3 million surplus on December 10 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON DECEMBER 10</p>
<p>Exports: $174.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $148.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $440.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $269.9 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $196.3 million</p>
<p>DECEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.440 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.343 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.152 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.227 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.022 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418</p>
</text>
